-- title:
--   Extension of an anemic eigensystem at squarefree level, with Uₚ a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ whose image in $\mathcal O$ lies in the maximal ideal, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$, and $N\geq 1$ a squarefree integer all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, such that for every prime $q\mid N$ with $q\neq p$ the representation $\bar\rho$ is not unramified at $q$, i.e. it is not the case that $\bar\rho.\rho$ kills the inertia subgroup over $\mathbb Q$ of every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q\in P.\mathrm{nonunits}$; assume also that the $\mathbb C$-span of the lattice of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is all of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$. Write $\mathbb T^{S'}=\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ N\ 2\ S'$ for the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S'$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S'$. Let $\theta\colon\mathbb T^{S}\to k$ be a ring homomorphism such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell\in P.\mathrm{nonunits}$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Finally let $S_0\subseteq S$ contain no prime divisor of $N$ and contain every $q\in S$ with $q\nmid N$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\theta'\colon\mathbb T^{S_0}\to k$, again with values in $k$ itself, which restricts to $\theta$ along the inclusion $\mathbb T^{S}\subseteq\mathbb T^{S_0}$ supplied by $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra\_mono}$, and which, in case $p\mid N$ and the $p$-adic Galois representation $\mathrm{GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep}\,\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ (for each valuation subring over $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule $L$ spanned by a member of a basis of $V$, stable under the decomposition subgroup, with $(\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma-1)V\subseteq L$ for $\sigma$ in inertia), satisfies $\theta'(U_p)\neq 0$.
--
--   This is the existence, at minimal squarefree level and with coefficients in the residue field $k$ itself, of the maximal ideal of the full Hecke algebra attached to $\bar\rho$, together with the unit-root normalisation $U_p\neq 0$ in the ordinary case; it extends an eigensystem given only on the anemic Hecke algebra away from $S$ to one including the operators $U_q$ at the primes dividing $N$. It is used to realise the localised Hecke algebra of $\bar\rho$ on a local corner of the cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$, at the foot of the level-raising argument.
-- source:
